In any game that I do altar camping the number of books I get
from that dominates the number of books that randomly appear
from other sources.  The numbers above only apply to random
appearances.  Interesting but if either spell is in a known
school an altar camper will be much more likely to see them.

Enchantment - Charm monster - skilled wizard, basic monk tourist.

Clerical - Create familiar - expert priest, skilled knight monk
samurai wizard.

Considering that spellbook gifts are based on spells not yet
known in unrestricted schools tourist has a far higher chance
of seeing the unrestricted charm monster than the restricted
create familiar, and priest knight samurai have a far higher
chance of seeing the unrestricted create familiar than the
restricted charm monster.

But play altar camping to the ridiculous and a character might
see every type of spellbook.  I once played a Valk altar camping
to the ridiculous and saw all books but one and nearly all of
the lawfull and unaligned artifacts as well.



